<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeju Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jejudo, Quelpart</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeju Island is a volcanic island off the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, the country's largest island, dominated by Mount Hallasan. It was the seat of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timna-yemen">Tamna</a> before its absorption by Goryeo, and in 1273 the last Sambyeolcho rebels were crushed there. In the Jeju uprising and its suppression in 1948–1949 tens of thousands of islanders were killed. It is now a self-governing province and a major resort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeju-island.jpg" alt="Jeju Island" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Simmon, using Landsat data provided by the United States Geological Survey. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeju_Island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
